  "schema": "transfer-reader-vector-endpoint-v1",
  "scope": "Core-only symbolic map/collect, in-place pending zip, length and exhaustive unspent-check proof. Individual status authentication has separate qualified readback evidence; no additional native control or full Transfer certification credit. Source hashes establish identity, not correspondence. Successful per-input lookup map/collect derives ordered alignment and exact result length. In-place pending zip preserves vector length, including excess suffixes for mismatched inputs; success of the actual reader supplies equality rather than assuming it. A successful stage-style zipped unspent check then covers every input and derives an observed false durable flag and false current pending membership. This does not assume an unspent poststate or supplied result-length law. Lookup denotes verified status at the captured boundary; individual authentication and actual Rust Vec/iterator/store correspondence remain separate interfaces. No cache mutation, native execution, atomic evidence refresh or full Transfer closure is claimed.",
  "toolchain_bytes_in_archive": 0
}
